==Reception==
The advantage has been met with mixed to negative reception. Former contestant [[Stephen Fishbach]] has derided the advantage as "one of the worst twists in show history" for undermining players' agency.<ref>https://twitter.com/stephenfishbach/status/1450984079466319874</ref> The introduction of the advantage in the fifth episode of an already twist-heavy {{S2|41}} also attracted a negative response.

While the advantage seeks to encourage its user to forge social connections to glean inside information, because of the advantage's co-existence with the [[Beware Advantage|Beware idols]] in both its appearances, this intention is defeated. By extension, the advantage has been viewed as overpowered since the public nature of the idols allows the advantage users to steal the idols without having to source for "knowledge" on who the idol holders are.<ref>https://robhasawebsite.com/survivor-42-episode-12-recap/ (2:22:00)</ref>

However, the advantage's outcome in ''41'', where the [[Yase Alliance]] outmaneuvered the advantage to hold their idol, has been commended as one of the highlights of the season.<ref>https://ew.com/tv/recaps/survivor-season-41-episode-7/</ref><ref>https://www.truedorktimes.com/s41/kaiser/e7.htm</ref> Similarly, the advantage's misplay in {{S2|42}} contributed to a [[Tribal Council]] which was also well-received.<ref>https://robhasawebsite.com/survivor-42-know-it-alls-episode-11-recap-live-915e-515p/</ref>

==Trivia==
* [[Geo Bustamante]] is the first castaway to be voted out while in possession of the Knowledge is Power advantage.
* Internationally, [[Myles Kuah]] is the first person to successfully play this advantage.
** [[Kristin Alston]] is the first person to have a Hidden Immunity Idol stolen by this advantage.
* Internationally, [[Parvati Shallow]] is the first person to willingly discard the Knowledge is Power advantage.
* The first two times the advantage was played:
** Multiple people had individual immunity at [[Tribal Council]], leaving exactly five people eligible for elimination.
** An [[Extra Vote]] was played.
** A [[Sydney Segal|wo]][[Drea Wheeler|man]] from a [[Luvu|bl]][[Ika|ue]] starting tribe was voted out.
** [[Xander Hastings|The]] [[Mike Turner|target]] made it to [[Final Tribal Council]] but did not win.

